## Assumptions and selection rule

- The fan and heat-sink pressure-drop curves intersect at a stable operating point.
- Air properties are constant at the stated values.
- The supplied fin-efficiency and effective-area models apply directly.
- Because no explicit optimization objective is given, I first eliminate all infeasible designs and then select the feasible design with the **lowest heat-sink mass, fan electrical power, and noise**. This gives the minimum-complexity feasible design.
- Fan F3 is immediately infeasible because its noise is \(57\ \mathrm{dBA}>53\ \mathrm{dBA}\).

